# Worktree local Supabase

## When local Supabase starts automatically

In `/.cursor/worktrees/`, `pnpm worktree:dev` calls `scripts/worktree-supabase-local.sh ensure` when **any** of:

1. `.worktree-local-supabase` marker exists (from a prior start in this worktree)
2. `USE_LOCAL_SUPABASE=1` is set
3. **Auto-detect:** `supabase/migrations/` differs from `origin/main` (new/changed migration files on this branch)
4. **Auto-detect:** `supabase migration list` shows migrations with **Local** set but **Remote** empty (merged to git but not yet `cloud-push` — e.g. Google Calendar tables missing on cloud)

Set `USE_LOCAL_SUPABASE=0` to skip auto-start even when migrations differ (use shared cloud dev instead).

## What the script does

`scripts/worktree-supabase-local.sh ensure` (preferred; idempotent):

1. Requires **Docker Desktop** running when branch migrations differ from `origin/main`
2. Starts local Supabase if not running
3. Verifies **required tables** for unpushed migrations (e.g. `google_calendar_connections`) exist
4. Runs **`supabase db reset`** only when tables are missing — applies migrations + **`supabase/seed.sql`**
5. Backs up cloud keys to `.env.local.cloud`, patches `.env.local` with local URL/anon key
6. Writes `.worktree-local-supabase` marker

`start` always runs a full reset (use when you explicitly want a clean DB).

See also **`worktree-unpushed-migrations-schema.mdc`** for schema cache error triage.

**Local dev sign-in:** one-click Judi/Savina picker, PIN **123456** / **654321**, or email fallback **devpassword123**. PIN rows seeded by `scripts/seed-local-dev-pins.mjs` after local `db reset`.

## During development (schema work)

- **Do NOT** `supabase db push` to the shared cloud project from a parallel worktree branch.
- Add migrations under `supabase/migrations/`; they apply locally via reset/start.
- Test against local Supabase (Studio: http://127.0.0.1:54323).

## Cloud project link (automatic)

`pnpm worktree:dev` runs `scripts/worktree-supabase-link.sh` on every worktree start:

- Reads project ref from **`supabase/cloud-project-ref`** (currently `xopqzujfcmtjwznyrjll`)
- Runs `supabase link --project-ref <ref> --yes` (no interactive picker)
- Skips if this worktree is already linked to the same ref
- Requires **`supabase login`** once per machine (CLI auth), not per worktree

Override ref: `SUPABASE_PROJECT_REF=otherref`. DB password (if prompted): `SUPABASE_DB_PASSWORD`.

## Manual commands

| Command | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `pnpm worktree:supabase:link` | Link/re-link cloud project (idempotent) |
| `pnpm worktree:supabase:ensure` | Verify local schema + patch `.env.local` (idempotent; use after schema cache errors) |
| `pnpm worktree:supabase:start` | Force local Supabase + full reset |
| `pnpm worktree:supabase:stop` | Stop local stack, restore cloud `.env.local` |
| `pnpm worktree:supabase:cloud-push` | Push migrations to linked **cloud** project (release) |

## Agents

- If the task adds/changes **schema/migrations**, ensure local Supabase is running (`pnpm worktree:dev` handles auto-start, or `pnpm worktree:supabase:start`).
- Never `repair` cloud migration history to work around parallel branches — use local Supabase instead.
